Chapter: ResizeMode
  cites Diffusion chapter Resize

 Forge's images.resize_image for img2img (modules/images.py, the upscaler
 None, so every resize is Pillow's LANCZOS) over RGB bytes. Mode 0 resizes to
 the target. Mode 1 resizes to cover it, the other side im.width * height //
 im.height or im.height * width // im.width as the aspect decides (ratio >
 src_ratio compared exactly as ow * h > w * oh), then pastes centred at
 (ow // 2 - sw // 2, oh // 2 - sh // 2), cropping what falls outside. Mode 2
 fits instead and fills the margins from the edges (below); any other mode is 0.

 We say:

Section: Paste

  rm-paste-row : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rm-paste-row (dst) (src) (di) (si) (n) (k) (z) =
    if k >= n then 0
    else rm-paste-row dst src di si n (k + 1) (poke-byte dst (di + k) (peek-byte src (si + k)))

  rm-paste : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rm-paste (dst) (ow) (oh) (src) (sw) (sh) (ox) (oy) (y) =
    if y >= oh then dst
    else let sy = y - oy
    in let x0 = if ox > 0 then ox else 0
    in let x1 = if ox + sw < ow then ox + sw else ow
    in let z = if sy >= 0 & sy < sh & x1 > x0 then rm-paste-row dst src ((y * ow + x0) * 3) ((sy * sw + x0 - ox) * 3) ((x1 - x0) * 3) 0 0 else 0
    in rm-paste dst ow oh src sw sh ox oy (y + 1)

Section: Modes

  resize-mode : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  resize-mode (mode) (src) (w) (h) (ow) (oh) =
    if mode == 0 then resize-lanczos src w h ow oh
    else if mode == 1 then
      (let sw = if ow * h > w * oh then ow else w * oh / h
       in let sh = if ow * h <= w * oh then oh else h * ow / w
       in rm-paste (alloc-bytes (ow * oh * 3 + 8)) ow oh (resize-lanczos src w h sw sh) sw sh (ow / 2 - sw / 2) (oh / 2 - sh / 2) 0)
    else if mode == 2 then rm-fill src w h ow oh
    else 0

Section: One Band

 An L picture (an inpaint mask) the same way: Pillow's L resize is the RGB
 arithmetic on one band, resize_image pastes into an RGB canvas for modes 1
 and 2, and every mode other than 0 and 1 takes the fill branch.

  rm-spread : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rm-spread (src) (d) (i) (n) = if i >= n then d else let v = peek-byte src (i / 3) in let z = poke-byte d i v in rm-spread src d (i + 1) n

  rm-band : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rm-band (src) (d) (i) (n) = if i >= n then d else let z = poke-byte d i (peek-byte src (i * 3)) in rm-band src d (i + 1) n

  resize-mode-l : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  resize-mode-l (mode) (src) (w) (h) (ow) (oh) =
    let rgb = resize-mode (if mode == 0 | mode == 1 then mode else 2) (rm-spread src (alloc-bytes (w * h * 3 + 8)) 0 (w * h * 3)) w h ow oh
    in if rgb == 0 then 0 else rm-band rgb (alloc-bytes (ow * oh + 8)) 0 (ow * oh)

Section: Fill

 Mode 2 fits, pastes centred on black, then fills each margin with Pillow's
 resize of a zero-size box at an edge (box=(0, 0, w, 0) and its kin). Forge
 passes no resample there, so Pillow 9.5 uses its default, BICUBIC (a = -0.5,
 support 2), not LANCZOS. The scale is 0, so every output line centres on that
 edge and takes the taps from int (e - 1.5) to int (e + 2.5), clamped.

  rm-repeat : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  rm-repeat (v) (n) (acc) = if list-length acc >= n then acc else rm-repeat v n (list-push acc v)

  rm-repeat-k : List Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  rm-repeat-k (k) (n) (i) (acc) = if i >= n then acc else rm-repeat-k k n (i + 1) (acc & k)

  rm-cubic : Real -> Real
  rm-cubic (v) =
    let x = if v < 0.0 then 0.0 - v else v
    in if x < 1.0 then (1.5 * x - 2.5) * x * x + 1.0
    else if x < 2.0 then (((x - 5.0) * x + 8.0) * x - 4.0) * (0.0 - 0.5)
    else 0.0

  rm-cubic-weights : Integer, Integer, Real, Real, List Real -> List Real
  rm-cubic-weights (x) (count) (xmin) (center) (acc) =
    if x >= count then acc
    else rm-cubic-weights (x + 1) count xmin center (list-push acc (rm-cubic (real-from-int x + xmin - center + 0.5)))

  rm-edge-axis : Integer, Integer, Integer -> RzAxis
  rm-edge-axis (insize) (outsize) (e) =
    let center = real-from-int e
    in let lo = rz-trunc (center - 2.0 + 0.5)
    in let xmin = if lo < 0 then 0 else lo
    in let hi = rz-trunc (center + 2.0 + 0.5)
    in let count = (if hi > insize then insize else hi) - xmin
    in let ws = rm-cubic-weights 0 count (real-from-int xmin) center []
    in let k = rz-push-k ws (rz-sum ws 0 0.0) 0 5 []
    in RzAxis { rz-min = rm-repeat xmin outsize [], rz-count = rm-repeat count outsize [], rz-k = rm-repeat-k k outsize 0 [], rz-ksize = 5 }

  rm-zero : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rm-zero (a) (n) (i) =
    if i >= n then a
    else let z = poke-byte a i 0
    in rm-zero a n (i + 1)

  rm-fill : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rm-fill (src) (w) (h) (ow) (oh) =
    let narrow = ow * h < w * oh
    in let sw = if narrow then ow else w * oh / h
    in let sh = if ow * h >= w * oh then oh else h * ow / w
    in let rs = resize-lanczos src w h sw sh
    in let dst = rm-paste (rm-zero (alloc-bytes (ow * oh * 3 + 8)) (ow * oh * 3) 0) ow oh rs sw sh (ow / 2 - sw / 2) (oh / 2 - sh / 2) 0
    in if narrow then
      (let fh = oh / 2 - sh / 2
       in if fh <= 0 then dst
       else let top = rz-vertical rs sw (alloc-bytes (sw * fh * 3 + 8)) fh (rm-edge-axis sh fh 0) 0 0
       in let bot = rz-vertical rs sw (alloc-bytes (sw * fh * 3 + 8)) fh (rm-edge-axis sh fh sh) 0 0
       in rm-paste (rm-paste dst ow oh top sw fh 0 0 0) ow oh bot sw fh 0 (fh + sh) 0)
    else if ow * h > w * oh then
      (let fw = ow / 2 - sw / 2
       in if fw <= 0 then dst
       else let lft = rz-horizontal rs sw 0 (alloc-bytes (fw * oh * 3 + 8)) fw (rm-edge-axis sw fw 0) oh 0
       in let rgt = rz-horizontal rs sw 0 (alloc-bytes (fw * oh * 3 + 8)) fw (rm-edge-axis sw fw sw) oh 0
       in rm-paste (rm-paste dst ow oh lft fw oh 0 0 0) ow oh rgt fw oh (fw + sw) 0 0)
    else dst
